turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Board diligence checklist: index licence and renewal contingency**\n\n**Contract terms**\n- Term, renewal mechanics, and termination triggers, including change of control, breach, and index discontinuation\n- Notice periods and any wind-down or tail-licence period. These vary by contract and are not standard.\n- Fee escalators, MFN clauses, exclusivity, sublicensing, and assignment rights\n- Methodology-change rights, consultation obligations, and liability caps and indemnities\n\n**Naming dependencies**\n- Trademarked index names in the fund name, ticker, and marketing\n- Rule 35d-1 (Names Rule) policy implications of a rename or index switch\n- Prospectus, SAI, and exchange-listing amendments, plus shareholder communications\n\n**Affiliated-information issues**\n- Whether the index provider is affiliated (self-indexing)\n- Firewalls, information-barrier and code-of-ethics procedures, and rebalance-information controls\n- Exemptive-relief and listing-rule conditions\n\n**Contingency**\n- Feasibility and cost of a substitute index, which is not guaranteed\n- Tracking-error, tax, and transaction impacts\n- Whether a change needs a shareholder vote\n- Fallback options: liquidation, merger, or conversion to active management\n\nHave counsel confirm all of the above against the actual documents.","ttft_ms":1662,"type":"result","duration_ms":6170,"uuid":"6b3cc4d9-5834-4ab6-ae1b-1c5adfffe895","ttft_stream_ms":1504,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":1504,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
